<p>The core of the AGI achievement is “Recursive-Logic-Synthesis.” Unlike legacy LLMs that relied on pattern-matching to provide a result, the AGI-tier model uses a <a href="/articles/meta-llama-4-open-frontier-release">massive context-reasoning window</a> to “verify and audit” its own thought-process in real-time. This allows the AI to perform “Active-Context-Chaining,” where it can autonomously <a href="/articles/ai-social-media-personalized-algorithms-2027">reason through a problem’s historical and emotional nuances</a> before drawing a conclusion. During the Turing-Test-v2, the AI was able to “maintain a consistent identity” over a 100-hour period of collaborative work in a Canvas 2 workspace, with human auditors unable to distinguish its reasoning from that of a top-tier domain expert.</p>
