<p>To maintain the safety and integrity of global trade, the Global Open-Source AI Safety Alliance has developed a new “Hardware-Ethic-Standard” for all ATL models. This standard includes “Kill-Switch-Inheritance,” which ensures that if a human owner revokes a sub-agent’s “Hardware-License,” the AI instantly stops all power-cycles and “locks-down” the chip’s location to prevent unauthorized changes. This “Sovereign Control” is a requirement for gaining the trust of enterprise clients in an era of automated intelligence and national security concerns.</p>
