<p>Beyond simple code review, Claude is also being used to help remodel some of the more legacy parts of the Firefox rendering engine. Browser engines are among the most complex pieces of software in existence, with millions of lines of code that have been written over decades. Claude’s massive 1-million-token context window allows it to “read” the entire codebase of specific modules, such as the CSS parser or the JavaScript JIT compiler, and suggest refactoring paths that improve performance while closing long-standing security “attack surfaces.” This helps Mozilla modernize its engine faster than would be possible with human developers alone.</p>
