<p>The headset also includes “Voice-Native System Control,” where the entire UI is designed to be navigated via natural conversation with a Llama-powered digital twin. Users can ask the headset to “find all the blue blueprints I was looking at yesterday” or “start a collaborative session with my team in London,” and the AI will handle the complex multi-app navigation and data retrieval. This shift away from traditional hand-tracked menus toward “Intent-Based Interaction” is what Meta believes will finally make VR/AR headsets accessible to the average consumer as a daily productivity tool.</p>
