<p>The alliance is also launching “The Open Safety Bounty,” a mult-million dollar fund provided by Meta and Mistral to reward developers who find and patch critical safety vulnerabilities in open-source models. This “Bug-Bounty-for-Intelligence” is familiar to the cybersecurity world and is intended to foster a new generation of “Safety Developers” who see alignment as a professional competitive field. By rewarding “discovery” over “denial,” the alliance aims to make open-source models the most secure and well-audited in the world—a philosophy echoed in Mark Zuckerberg’s Open Intelligence Manifesto.</p>
