<p>The engine’s “Publisher-First” design is a key part of OpenAI’s strategy to win over the media industry. Each answer includes prominent links to the original sources, and OpenAI has established revenue-sharing agreements with major publishers like Condé Nast and The Associated Press. A new “Publisher Control Panel” allows site owners to manage exactly how their content is summarized and cited, addressing long-standing concerns about AI “cannibalizing” web traffic. By creating a collaborative rather than adversarial relationship with content creators, OpenAI hopes to build a more sustainable and high-quality index than its predecessors.</p>
