<p>OpenAI is also introducing “Personalized Discovery,” which uses the model’s understanding of a user’s interests (stored within its long-term memory system) to surface relevant news and research without a direct query. This “push-not-pull” model of information discovery aims to compete with Google Discover and various social media feeds, providing a more curated and signal-dense alternative to the current ad-heavy information landscape. By focusing on deep, factual relevance rather than engagement-maximizing algorithms, OpenAI is betting that users are ready for a more quiet and functional way to explore the digital world.</p>
