<p>This update also carries a significant cost benefit. By eliminating the need for “repeat requests” due to formatting errors, developers can achieve their desired outcome with fewer total tokens. OpenAI has further optimized the “pre-fill” latency for schemas, ensuring that even large and complex JSON definitions do not significantly impact the time-to-first-token. This focus on “low-latency, high-reliability” data extraction is a key part of OpenAI’s strategy to become the foundational layer for the next wave of “agentic” micro-services, where <a href="/articles/openai-gpt-5-extended-reasoning">GPT-5</a> acts as a high-speed data processor for thousands of interconnected business apps.</p>
